{"id":"2026-11-22-CME","date":"2026-11-22","ticker":"CME","name":"CME Group","sector":"Financials","industry":"Financial Data & Stock Exchanges","price":307.56,"price_date":"2026-11-20","timeframe_days":182,"headline":"CME's revenue growth bounced back to 13% on record trading, and its market data business grew for the 34th quarter in a row","side":"long","timeframe":"About 6 months, through the next two quarterly reports","thesis":"CME's revenue growth went from 1% in the June quarter back to 13% in September, on a record 29.4M contracts traded a day, up 16%. Trading grew by double digits in all six product groups, and international trading rose 22% to 9M contracts a day. The market data business, which sells price feeds to banks and trading firms, grew 20% to a record $243M, its 34th straight quarter of growth. Adjusted earnings per share rose 13% to $3.02. Interest rate shifts, wars and trade disputes keep hedgers busy, and CME owns most of the world's benchmark futures. The stock is above both of its averages and beat the S&P 500 by 22 points over three months.","wrong_if":"A close under 283 would break the 200-day average and the idea would be over. It is also wrong if daily volume falls back below the year-ago level for two months in a row, or if a court ruling or a rival exchange forces CME to cut fees.","business":"CME Group runs the world's largest futures exchange. Traders and companies use its contracts to bet on or protect against moves in interest rates, stock indexes, oil, gas, metals, crops and currencies. CME earns a fee on every contract traded and cleared, sells market data, and holds customers' collateral. It owns the Chicago Mercantile Exchange, the Chicago Board of Trade, NYMEX and COMEX.","segments_note":"Clearing and trading fees, about 80% of revenue at $1.4B, grew 12% in the September quarter after falling 3% in June, so they drive the speed-up. Market data grew 20%, near its fastest pace in the table, and has grown every quarter for more than eight years. Other revenue, mostly fees on collateral, grew 8%.","growth_note":"Revenue was $1.74B, up 13%, after 15% in March and 1% in June, so growth is uneven and depends on how busy markets are. Adjusted earnings per share rose 13% to $3.02. The June dip came against a very busy quarter a year earlier, so the second half of 2026 looks cleaner. Missing: the brief's guidance table is empty, so there are no company targets to check against.","commentary":[{"point":"Record September quarter volume of 29.4M contracts a day, up 16%, with double-digit growth in all six product groups.","speaker":"Terry Duffy, chairman and CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Record revenue for a September quarter and a new all-time high for market data at $243M. Stock index trading rose 23%.","speaker":"Lynne Fitzpatrick, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"International trading averaged 9M contracts a day, up 22%, with commercial momentum in more than 50 countries.","speaker":"CME management","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"New single stock futures got off to a strong start, with fast uptake in Europe and Asia where traders already know the product.","speaker":"Tim McCourt, head of equity and currency products","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"},{"point":"Said they are confident in their position in a pending court case and expect it to be fully argued before the judge in December.","speaker":"Terry Duffy, chairman and CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"},{"point":"Said there is great momentum heading into the end of the year.","speaker":"Julie Winkler, chief commercial officer","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"}],"tone_note":"Net tone rose by about 19 points from the call before and hedging words fell by about 24, so management sounded more sure of itself. The one area they were careful about was the court case, which they said they expect to win but did not explain in detail.","technical_note":"The stock closed at 307.56, above its 50-day average (289.43) and 200-day average (282.02). It has risen 11% in three months, beating the S&P 500 by 22 points and financial stocks by 18, while RSI at 55 shows it is not stretched. Volume is normal. The 52-week high is 329.16.","valuation_note":"At 25.3 times trailing earnings, CME is above its median of 23.8 and close to the 80th percentile of 25.7, so it is not cheap. This idea depends on earnings growth carrying the stock, not on the multiple rising. A quiet market would hit both.","levels":{"entry_lo":298,"entry_hi":312,"stop":283,"target":347,"note":"Buy between 298 and 312, between the 50-day average and the current price. The stop at 283 sits just under the 200-day average. The target of 347 is about 5% above the 52-week high and needs about 13% earnings growth at today's multiple. From the posted price that is about $39 of upside for $25 of risk, or 1.6 to 1."},"risks":["Trading volume rises when markets are nervous and falls when they calm down. A quiet stretch would slow growth fast.","The stock is near the top of its normal price-to-earnings range, so any slowdown could cut the multiple too.","Management flagged a fee impact of about 0.5% to 1% from changes to its pricing.","A pending court case could affect part of the business; the brief does not give its details.","New exchanges and crypto platforms are trying to win futures trading."],"catalysts":["Monthly volume reports, released in the first days of each month.","The court hearing in December that management mentioned.","The December quarter report, likely in early February 2027, and any 2027 fee or cost plan.","Federal Reserve meetings, which drive interest rate futures trading."],"facts":{"financials":{"updated":"2026-11-18","adj_eps_name":"Adjusted EPS","quarters":[{"q":"Dec '23","id":"FY2023Q4","end":"2023-12-31","rev":1439.3,"gm":null,"om":60.0,"nm":58.7,"eps":2.35,"adj_eps":2.37,"rev_yoy":19.2,"eps_yoy":23.4},{"q":"Mar '24","id":"FY2024Q1","end":"2024-03-31","rev":1487.9,"gm":null,"om":64.5,"nm":56